 "prompt_sha256": "fdb63ae38a23c81771528cfaa6a0473c497c5c5b0d0adf8bfb13b2e9db9b1523",
 "answer": "To re-run only the promptfoo test cases that ended in an error, you can use the `promptfoo retry` command. This command is specifically designed to retry all test cases that resulted in errors, such as those caused by network issues, rate limits, or API failures. Here’s how you can use it:\n\n1. **Retry Errors for a Specific Eval:**\n   If you have a specific evaluation ID and want to retry the test cases that resulted in errors, use:\n   ```sh\n   promptfoo retry <evalId>\n   ```\n   Replace `<evalId>` with the ID of your evaluation.\n\n2. **Retry Errors for the Latest Eval:**\n   If you want to retry the errors from the latest evaluation, use:\n   ```sh\n   promptfoo eval --retry-errors\n   ```\n   This command finds and retries all ERROR results from the most recent evaluation.\n\n### Additional Options:\n- **Different Configuration File:**\n  You can specify a different configuration file for the retry operation:\n  ```sh\n  promptfoo retry eval-abc123 -c updated-config.yaml\n  ```\n\n- **Verbose Output and Concurrency:**\n  For more detailed output and to limit concurrency:\n  ```sh\n  promptfoo retry eval-abc123 -v --max-concurrency 2\n  ```\n\n- **Share Results to Cloud:**\n  To share the results after retrying:\n  ```sh\n  promptfoo retry eval-abc123 --share\n  ```\n\n### Important Notes:\n- **Data Safety:** If the retry operation fails, your original ERROR results are preserved. You can re-run the retry command safely, and old ERROR results are only removed after a successful retry.\n- **Flag Restrictions:** The `--retry-errors` feature cannot be used together with `--resume` or `--no-write` flags.\n\nUsing these commands, you can efficiently manage and retry only those test cases that encountered errors, ensuring that your evaluations are complete and accurate.",
